.TH KTX_DEFLATE 1 "2026-10-27" "ktx (Rust port)" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ktx_deflate \- supercompress a KTX2 file
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ktx
deflate [OPTION...] <input\-file> <output\-file>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Applies zstd or zlib supercompression to the levels of a KTX2 file. Files that are already
supercompressed are recompressed. Basis\-LZ textures cannot be deflated.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-zstd <level>
Zstandard level, 1 to 22.
.TP
.B \-\-zlib <level>
zlib level, 1 to 9.
.TP
.B \-\-quiet
Do not print warnings.
.TP
.B \-\-warnings\-as\-errors
Treat warnings as errors.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
.nf
ktx deflate \-\-zstd 18 in.ktx2 out.ktx2
.fi
.SH NOTES
This is an unofficial Rust port of Khronos KTX\-Software (libktx and the ktx CLI); it is not
the Khronos build of the tool. The complete, current option list is printed by
.B ktx deflate \-\-help.
.SH SEE ALSO
ktx(1)
